[{"finding":"When a value crosses a process/language boundary to multiple consumers, fix moves to the consumers, never to the emitter — the emitter's spelling is treated as fixed even when it predates the consumers","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:40"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-boundary consistency test derives its expected value by parsing the authoritative source's own literal, rather than trusting a second constant hand-copied beside it","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/capture/dispatch-action.test.ts:29"],"released":false},{"finding":"When historical records violate a newly-introduced invariant and cannot be repaired, the entries that violate it are dropped with a logged count, and the pipeline proceeds on the resulting wider approximation rather than failing the run","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:130"],"released":false},{"finding":"A trigger gate is chosen from the event field that identifies who performed the act (sender/author_association) rather than a label or state that anyone can cause to exist.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/shape.yml:44"],"released":false},{"finding":"When repairing a stale citation, the session sometimes resolved the surrounding claim's substance (introducing a new \"decided\" state, e.g. branch protection declined) rather than only replacing the dead pointer, without flagging that as a separate judgement call.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/gauntlet-hook.mjs:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"When removing a locally-mirrored artifact whose canonical copy lives at an external URL, delete the local citation path entirely rather than keeping it alongside the URL","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["GOAL.md:227"],"released":false},{"finding":"Test doubles for two dependencies whose relative order matters are logged into one shared call-sequence array rather than separate counters, so ordering assertions read off a single list.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/back-stamp.test.ts:233"],"released":false},{"finding":"Assertions over a corpus that can grow over time are expressed as properties (plus their logical converse) instead of a pinned literal count, so the test doesn't go red merely because the corpus grew.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/missing-trailer.test.ts:96"],"released":false},{"finding":"A non-gate helper degrades by skipping work it can't complete rather than failing outright, reserving fail-closed behavior for the actual gate that will catch the same problem downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/new-adr:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"A file meant partly for model injection separates human-facing explanatory prose from the injected content behind a delimiter, and the accessor throws rather than silently returning an empty or over-inclusive result if the split fails","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:286"],"released":false},{"finding":"A small error-preserving-and-rethrow wrapper is duplicated at a second failure site instead of generalized into one shared helper, despite the new function's own comment describing it as making \"the same bargain\" as the existing one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:393"],"released":false},{"finding":"A test's fixture parser splits on a maximally permissive delimiter and asserts shape explicitly afterward, rather than matching a pattern that could silently skip a malformed entry","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/vocabulary.test.ts:21"],"released":false},{"finding":"Validate every item in a batch before performing any side effect on any of them, so a single invalid item leaves zero effects rather than a partial write.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:138"],"released":false},{"finding":"When two options represent mutually exclusive semantics, refuse the call at the very top of the function before any other work runs, rather than picking a resolution order between them.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.ts:285"],"released":false},{"finding":"A gate that can silently drop a true positive must be built from deterministic lookups against already-produced artifacts rather than a model's judgement, because a wrong drop is invisible downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/structural-refusal.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `gh`-workflow-YAML test reads and parses the workflow file directly (`readFileSync` + `yaml.parse`) instead of using the shared `readWorkflow` helper this diff introduces for exactly that purpose, unlike every sibling workflow test in the same diff.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/review.test.ts:296"],"released":false},{"finding":"Parsing the issue number back out of `gh issue create`'s stdout (a `/\\/issues\\/(\\d+)\\s*$/`-style regex plus a \"could not parse an issue number\" throw) is reimplemented verbatim per module instead of being factored into one shared helper.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/publish-findings.ts:16"],"released":false},{"finding":"Cross-lane dispatch event-type constants get exactly one declaration, and are guarded by a test that reads the wire name out of every receiving workflow's `if:` and checks it against that single constant, rather than each side testing its own imported copy.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/immutable-set.test.ts:135"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `repository_dispatch` trigger branch carries no separate sender/actor authorization check (no `sender.login` or `author_association` gate), because sending the dispatch itself already required write access, so the send is treated as the authorization.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/spec-workflow.test.ts:75"],"released":false},{"finding":"A dispatch payload field's encoding (comma-joined string vs. repeated `key[]=` array) is chosen based on how the specific downstream job parses it — comma-joined for a shell string-compare job, a real repeated array for a job that reads it as JSON.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.ts:300"],"released":false},{"finding":"An issue's label is applied on the same `gh issue create` call that files it, never as a follow-up `issue edit`, so the issue is never observable in an unlabeled state that other automation could read as an ordinary issue.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:139"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-call ordering guarantee is tested by comparing call indices (`findIndex`/`toBeGreaterThan`) to prove one action happened strictly after another, rather than asserting only that both calls occurred.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shape/accept.test.ts:291"],"released":false},{"finding":"An exemption from an automated reachability/dead-code gate must carry an inline prose reason at the exemption site itself, never a silent name in an ignore list","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:57",".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:93","knip.config.ts:79"],"released":true},{"finding":"A baseline that grandfathers existing debt into a new gate must only ratchet down and gate solely on new additions, never re-grow or serve as a permanent allowlist","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/wiring-baseline.json:3","docs/agents/clone-gate.md:46"],"released":true},{"finding":"A check-command allowlist keyed to specific remote-reading commands (gh api/issue/pr/run, curl, wget), not a broader \"reaches outside the repository\" heuristic, because a deliberately-outside-repo but locally-readable path must still pass","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.ts:33"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a test double must echo back untrusted string content that may contain shell metacharacters, write it to a file the stub reads back rather than interpolating it into the stub script's own source","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.test.ts:76"],"released":false},{"finding":"Context a model needs for correctness is inlined directly into its prompt rather than granted through a tool or allow-list, so its reach is a fact about what was built rather than an instruction it must choose to honor.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:95"],"released":false},{"finding":"Content rendered into a prompt for a model is left uncapped rather than truncated, since a partial view recreates the same guessing problem the full view was added to remove.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"Structurally distinct absent-states (a claimed file not yet created vs. a ticket that claims no files at all) are given separate, explicit sentinel messages rather than collapsed into one empty or undefined representation.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A body-section parser is relocated to the shared module that owns the data shape it reads, once a second caller needs the same reading, rather than staying in the file of whichever caller wrote it first.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/ticket-shape.ts:176"],"released":false},{"finding":"A structural text matcher built to read a config/workflow file strips comments before matching, because prose explaining a decision can itself contain text indistinguishable from a real match.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["tests/acceptance/workflow-shape.fixture.ts:94"],"released":false},{"finding":"A counter that recomputes its entire result set from scratch every run is entitled to close its own standing issue when the count reaches zero, but a counter that only sees a partial slice of state per run must not, since it lacks the full picture to justify closing.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:341"],"released":false},{"finding":"A failure in a side-effecting close/retire call is caught, logged, and dropped rather than surfaced as a run failure, because the operation is idempotent and the next scheduled run will naturally retry it.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:354"],"released":false},{"finding":"When an action posts a record that justifies a subsequent state-changing call to an external system, the record-writing call must be ordered before the state-changing call, so a downstream reader of history never observes the change without its justification already present.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:351"],"released":false},{"finding":"A CI checkout must use fetch-depth: 0 whenever the job runs a test suite that may assert facts about git history rather than the working tree, since shallow clones make history-dependent checks fail on venue artefacts rather than real facts","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:112"],"released":false},{"finding":"Machine-written trailers/markers must be stripped from content before it's shown to a model and deterministically re-appended after the model's output is written back, rather than trusting the model to preserve them verbatim","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:131"],"released":false},{"finding":"A scripted test fake with an ordered list of per-call responses should throw once it runs out of responses rather than silently repeating the last one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.fake.ts:37"],"released":false},{"finding":"When new work must happen between a decision and its effects, split a combined decide-and-apply function into a pure counting/deciding half and a single shared applying half, rather than duplicating the apply logic per caller","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stage that revises output already validated by an earlier decision should not have that decision re-checked against its output, since there is no remaining channel to resolve a fresh objection","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:416"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a stage's structured output is naturally a single scalar value, wrap it with a scalar-rooted output schema instead of modeling it as a synthetic single-field object type","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/reconcile.ts:56"],"released":false},{"finding":"A repair lane declines and returns early rather than running a model when it cannot reproduce the failure it was dispatched to fix.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"An optional repair step that fails is logged and skipped rather than failing the run, leaving the actual gate that cares about it to report the staleness by name.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/regenerate-artifacts.ts:84"],"released":false},{"finding":"A caught subprocess failure is classified by reading the resulting state (e.g. git's unmerged index) rather than by matching the exception's message text.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:386"],"released":false},{"finding":"An outcome that records an external condition rather than a verdict on the work itself leaves the run's exit code green, while every other refusal reddens it.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:622"],"released":false},{"finding":"A fail-closed mechanism memoizes a repeated subprocess call so its total worst-case latency stays under its own enforced timeout, rather than letting a timeout silently convert fail-closed into fail-open.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/close-gate.py:487"],"released":false},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — \"the why behind a shared helper lives once, in the helper's docstring (or the ADR)... Red flag: a comment outside the helper's home that explains what the helper used to do... or why sharing fixed it.\" This test-file docstring restates the full #195/#233/#253 story of why `undelivered` moved off `ClosedEvent.closer` onto `closedByPullRequestsReferences` — the same story already told in `undelivered`'s own docstring in `bin/close-ticket`.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/close-ticket.test.ts:9"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Test the public interface** — \"test through the module's public surface, never its internals... Red flag: a test importing a private helper or a server-internal module directly.\" This loads `bin/close-ticket` as a module through a custom Python loader and calls `module.undelivered(...)` directly, bypassing the CLI's own `--spec` invocation, which is the tool's actual public surface.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/close-ticket.test.ts:56"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — this test comment restates ADR-0111's own evidence (the exact #233 dates/times and run counts) rather than naming the ADR and stopping; a citation follows, but only after the story is retold in full.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/workflow-permissions.test.ts:424"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — this workflow comment restates ADR-0111's evidence (the #233 date/time detail) almost verbatim rather than citing the ADR by number alone.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".github/workflows/spec.yml:85"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — this test comment retells the rationale for regenerating generated artifacts (the ADR-0107/run-33284271370/472KB story) that already lives in `regenerate-artifacts.ts`'s own docstring, rather than only naming the helper and ticket/ADR.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.test.ts:373"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — this describe-block comment retells `rebaseOntoTrunk`'s own rationale (the #183/#234 story of why a conflict is returned rather than thrown) that already lives in `integrate.ts`'s docstring for that function.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.test.ts:661"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — this describe-block comment retells the rationale for `fixer.yml`'s existence (the #169/#183/#234 unwired-lane story) that already lives in `fixer.yml`'s own header comment.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:210"],"released":true}]
